>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `xtraversedata_for_ss`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.xtraversedata_for_ss :
  simpExtLib.simpset -> TraverseExt.xtraverse_data
simpExtLib.traversedata_for_ss :
  simpExtLib.simpset -> TraverseExt.traverse_data
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Extracts the traversal data of an extension simpset.

`xtraversedata_for_ss ss` returns the rewriters, decision procedures,
congruence rules and limit of `ss`, paired with its subgoaler, unsafe
solvers, side-condition depth and term order, for use with
`TraverseExt.XTRAVERSE`. `traversedata_for_ss ss` returns the same data
without these settings, for use with `TraverseExt.TRAVERSE`.

Bounded rewrites (`Once`, `Ntimes`) share their remaining uses with those
of `ss`.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.set_cond_depth 2
     (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss);
>> TraverseExt.XTRAVERSE (simpExtLib.xtraversedata_for_ss ss) [] “T ∧ p”;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpExtLib.set_cond_depth),
[`TraverseExt.CONFIG_REDUCER`](#TraverseExt.CONFIG_REDUCER),
[`simpExtLib.mk_simpset`](#simpExtLib.mk_simpset).
